Thanks :) How to change a directory name so the first char is a lower case from the gui?
ChatGPT sade:
On macOS you can do it from the GUI, but there’s one trick: Finder normally prevents renaming only by changing the case, because it thinks the name didn’t actually change.

Here’s how to force the first character to become lowercase using the macOS GUI:

✅ Method 1 — Rename to a temporary name (the workaround)
Select the directory in Finder.

Press Return to rename it.

Change it to a different name entirely (e.g., add a character).
Example:

From: FolderName

To: TempFolderName

Press Return again.

Now rename it to the version with the lowercase letter.
Example:

From: TempFolderName

To: folderName

✔ This works because Finder now sees it as a meaningful change.

👍 Method 2 — Use “Get Info” (also a workaround)
Right-click the folder → Get Info.

In the “Name & Extension” field, rename it to something else first.

Press Enter.

Rename it again to the lowercase version.

❗ Why Finder won’t let you directly change case
macOS uses a case-insensitive filesystem by default, so:
FolderName and folderName → treated as the same name unless it’s first made “different.”

